  "keyTakeaways": [
    "Canada and Mexico take 72% of U.S. vegetable exports and charge nothing under USMCA. Canada’s 2025 counter-tariff on U.S. tomatoes and fresh beans ended on September 1, 2025, and its 2026 counter-tariffs skip vegetables.",
    "Pulses are the trade-policy story: exports of dry beans, lentils, dried peas and chickpeas fell 30.6% to $973 million in 2025. India charges 30% on yellow peas and China about 42–48% on U.S. pulses.",
    "The EU is opening up: since July 1, 2026 U.S. onions, fresh sweet potatoes, asparagus, sweet peppers, fresh beans and some dried and frozen vegetables enter duty-free, on top of the EU’s 0% on pulses.",
    "Dates to watch: China’s 24-point suspension ends January 10, 2027 (U.S. dried peas would go from 42.5% to 66.5%), and India’s free-import window for yellow peas ends March 31, 2027."
  ],
